        ],
        "text": "According to Petitioners, in 1986 Congress converted worker\u2011authorization regulation from a peripheral to a core concern of immigration policy by enacting the Immigration Reform and Control Act."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "United States (Amicus Curiae)",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "32e8c22bc0e45e925c75b29cd5725f46c7eec3c75ac79c5e0616fe94c59e4f41",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-32e8c22bc0e4-0000-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 20,
              "start": 20
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to United States (Amicus Curiae), according to United States (Amicus Curiae), according to United States (Amicus Curiae), congress declared federal employer sanctions to be central to immigration law, pre\u2011empting most state and local sanctions except limited licensing provisions."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Phillips",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "32e8c22bc0e45e925c75b29cd5725f46c7eec3c75ac79c5e0616fe94c59e4f41",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-32e8c22bc0e4-0003-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 57,
              "start": 57
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Phillips, congress sought to balance minimizing employer burdens, preventing discrimination, and avoiding the hiring of unauthorized workers."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "32e8c22bc0e45e925c75b29cd5725f46c7eec3c75ac79c5e0616fe94c59e4f41",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-32e8c22bc0e4-0003-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 57,
              "start": 57
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Under the federal scheme, a state may revoke a professional license if the licensee is convicted of a federal immigration crime."
      }
    ],
